<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Telia says has made HDTV breakthrough.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Telia says has made HDTV breakthrough.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's state-owned telecoms operator Telia said on Thursday it had reached a technology breakthrough that made it possible for the first time to send High Definition Television (HDTV) over normal telephone lines.</p>
<p>&quot;Every household can get an electronic motorway straight through their living room without needing any new cables,&quot; Telia said in a statement,</p>
<p>&quot;This will be in commercial operation by next year.&quot;</p>
<p>Telia is to hold a press demonstration of the new technology on April 4.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
